# Round XI Track M — KNOWN GAP (D36 unimplemented, HIGH).
#
# Class 1 of 4 filed by Track M: CHAINED `.method()` on a Guard[Trait] receiver
# passes the checker (surprising — the checker's auto-deref logic accepts it)
# and reaches C-emit which FABRICATES a runtime call `gorget_guard_greet`
# that has no runtime definition, causing a hard C-compile error.
#
# Under D36 (ratified 2026-07-27, `docs/define-gorget/decisions.md:1363-1381`)
# the read face `.method()` with `&Inner` self MUST accept + auto-deref
# uniformly for Guard + ReadGuard + WriteGuard + Box. This fixture pins the
# bare-trait shape; the Box variant `Mutex[Box[Speaker]](Box.new(...)).lock()
# .greet()` collapses to the SAME fabricated symbol at C-emit (pass-5 probe
# verified `gorget_guard_greet`, not a distinct `gorget_guard_box_greet`),
# so ONE fixture pins this class. The shape asymmetry between bare-trait and
# Box variants surfaces in the check-REJECT of the NAMED form (see class 2 /
# guard_trait_named_reject/).
#
# DISTINCT FROM Track J (`sound_guard_get_string_double_free.gg` — heap-inner
# ownership on non-trait inners; different root — `.get()` returns owned Str
# treated as owned local, double-freed at scope exit). This class is about
# TRAIT dispatch on the Guard wrapper, not heap-inner ownership.
#
# HEAD behavior (probe 2026-07-28):
#   gg check <this>            → OK: no semantic errors (exit 0)
#   gg build <this> -o /tmp/p  → C-emit stage error (printed to stderr,
#     wrapper still exits 0 — Core #15(d) probe note):
#     implicit declaration of function 'gorget_guard_greet'
#     C compiler exited with: exit status: 1
#     (C source generated at /tmp/p.c line 3442; no binary produced)
#
# FIX DIRECTION (Option A / D36-implementation, DEFERRED to Round XII+):
# extend `method_resolutions` value per D36 Q2 to
# `{ def_id, auto_deref: Option<DerefWrapperKind> }`, add a Guard vtable
# dispatch branch mirroring Box in `src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs:1627-1682`.
#
# INTENDED (after Option A): prints `beep R2`.

trait Speaker:
    String greet(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String greet(self):
        return "beep " + self.name

void main():
    print(Mutex[Speaker](Robot("R2")).lock().greet())
